  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Rural Entrepreneurship Assistance Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The goal of REAP is to help increase household income, and access to finance and markets. The project will provide business skills training and micro-loans (repayable through VSLAs) allowing people to establish small businesses and strengthen existing businesses. REAP will work towards lifting 5250 households in the Mulanje and Phalombe District of Malawi out of extreme poverty by 2025. The goal is transforming the lives of thousands by taking concrete steps towards ending extreme poverty.
The specific objectives are: 
Outcome 1: Increased financial inclusion and economic opportunities of 5250 poor households of which 70 % are women and 30% are men.&#xa0;
Activities
1.1.1 Targeting &#x2013; through community led participatory approach. Identify new REAP participants through community consultation, ranking through REAP unique targeting tool.
1.1.2 Support for the formation of &#xa0;350 VSLAs
1.1.3 Skills transfer through business skills training, VSLA and finacial literacy training.
1.1.4 Further training for VSLAs in group dynamics and provision of technical assistance on group functionality.
1.1.5 Disburse zero interest loans through VSLAs as start-up capital&#xa0;
1.1.6 VSLA interest free loan repayments and graduation.
1.1.7 Life-skills sessions include household decision-making, the importance of educating children, family planning, natural resource management, health and women&#x2019;s rights. &#xa0;
Outcome 2: Increased and diversified livelihood practices by 5250 poor households of which 70%&#xa0; are women and 30% are men.
Activities
2.1.1 Promote and support selected 50 graduated groups in businesses of their choice both with quick turn around &#xa0;fish farming, small livestock production, horticulture, bee keeping e.t.c
2.1.2 VSLAs produce group business plans and submit for funding. Some of the businesses that show greatest potential are selected for further loan funding for expansion.
2.1.3 Provision loans &#xa0;for &#xa0;both enterprises that require high investments or Expanded turnover as well as those with quick turnover businesses.
Monitoring,Evaluation and Learning 
1.1.1 Conduct baseline survey of the project.
1.1.2 Conduct routine Programme (data quality audits) and finance Monitoring.
1.1.3 Quartery review meeting.
1.1.4 Conduct annual outcome performance survey.
1.1.5 Conduct endterm evaluation.</narrative>
  </description>
